==============================================================================
E. PREFILL — decode-rate, as today
==============================================================================
  There is no batched prefill in this design (RD9_GATE 16 item 5;
  ARCHITECTURE.md 'weight-stationary batched prefill' is listed as
  orthogonal and untouched).  A P-token prompt therefore costs P x
  the decode step above, minus the LM head, on whichever board(s)
  hold the layers.  A weight-stationary batched prefill would make
  the matvec term amortise over the batch and leave the layer and
  link terms per token — label E, unquantified here, and WORTH MORE
  at these step times than it was at 2B, for the same reason the
  4B/9B study gave (its section 6 item 7).
